{% layout "layout.glaze" title: "Install", current: "/install" %}
<article class="prose">
<h1>Install Kiln</h1>
<p>Kiln is one executable that needs nothing else installed. The installers download the latest release, check its SHA-256 checksum and put <code>kiln</code> in <code>~/.kiln/bin</code>, on your PATH.</p>
<h2 id="linux">Linux</h2>
<Copy text="curl --proto '=https' --tlsv1.2 -sSf https://raw.githubusercontent.com/IZ737/kiln/main/install.sh | sh" client:visible />
<p>The default location belongs to your user and needs no administrator permissions. To select version 0.10.0 and that location explicitly:</p>
<Copy text={"curl --proto '=https' --tlsv1.2 -sSf https://raw.githubusercontent.com/IZ737/kiln/main/install.sh | sh -s -- --version v0.10.0 --dir \"$HOME/.kiln\""} client:visible />
<p>Choose a directory you can write to. In a restricted cloud workspace, use <code>--dir /workspace/.kiln --no-modify-path</code>, then run <code>export PATH=&quot;/workspace/.kiln/bin:$PATH&quot;</code> in your shell. <code>/opt/kiln</code> usually requires administrator permissions.</p>
<h2 id="windows">Windows</h2>
<p>In PowerShell:</p>
<Copy text="irm https://raw.githubusercontent.com/IZ737/kiln/main/install.ps1 | iex" client:visible />
<h2 id="upgrading">Upgrading</h2>
<p>You run the installer once. After that, <code>kiln upgrade</code> replaces kiln with the latest release:</p>
<pre><code>kiln upgrade            # the latest release
kiln upgrade --check    # only say whether there is a newer one</code></pre>
<h2 id="editors">Editors</h2>
<p>Each release has a VS Code extension, and other editors use <code>kiln lsp</code>: see <a href="/docs/guides/editors">editor setup</a>.</p>
<p>Next: <a href="/start">write your first program</a>.</p>
</article>
